p' src/cljc/yin/vm; sed -n '2133,2168p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc; sed -n '1235,1263p' src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git diff --name-status adb6af80..ff8b980a\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2444:(defn- heap-write\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2450:  (update-in state [:heap id] (fn [entry] (assoc entry :value v, :seal seal))))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2784:            {:state (heap-write s' id (:seal ref) (:val effect)),\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2795:            {:state (heap-write state id (get-in state [:heap id :seal])\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2817:            {:state (assoc-in s' [:heap id] {:value (:val effect),\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:123:**Provenance:** an entry may carry an optional private `:provenance` sibling beside `:value` and `:seal`, written only by the privileged mint (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, effect `:cell/new-provenance`) at allocation, never attached, replaced, or cleared afterwards. The VM treats it as opaque data — no frontend dispatch, no reason matching, no rendering — and answers it only through the authenticated private reader (`cell/dsg__provenance`, effect `:cell/provenance`), which returns nil for anything else and is never fatal. `cell/get` returns only `:value`; `cell/set!` and `heap-write` preserve `:provenance` while updating `:value`/`:seal`. The collector traces `:provenance` as data from every live entry, from pinned entries, and as an extra root at allocation, so payload cells referenced only by a retained provenance stay reachable while the wrapper is, and become collectible when the wrapper drops.\\n  \\\"Compile a Clojure form to Universal AST.\\n\\n  This is the main entry point that dispatches to specific compilers\\n  based on the form type.\\n\\n  macro-env: compile-time map of defmacro names in scope. A macro call is an\\n  ordinary application; macro-env only stops the native defn lowering.\\\"\\n  [form tail? env macro-env top?]\\n  (cond\\n    ;; Literals: constants self-evaluate; collections with dynamic elements\\n    ;; lower to constructor calls so their elements evaluate like Clojure\\n    (literal? form)\\n    (if (constant-form? form)\\n      (compile-literal form tail?)\\n      (compile-constructed-collection form tail? env macro-env))\\n    ;; The empty list is self-evaluating data, not an application\\n    (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) (compile-literal form tail?)\\n    ;; Variables (symbols)\\n    (symbol? form) (if (native-name? env form)\\n                     (if (outcomes? env)\\n                       (compile-call-descriptor (compile-adapter form env false macro-env) tail?)\\n                       (compile-adapter form env tail? macro-env))\\n                     (compile-variable form tail?))\\n    ;; Special forms and function application\\n    (seq? form)\\n    (let [[operator & operands] form]\\n      (cond\\n        ;; dao.stream.apply call: (dao.stream.apply/call :op/name arg1 arg2)\\n        (= operator 'dao.stream.apply/call)\\n        (let [[op & args] operands]\\n          (compile-dao-stream-apply-call op args env tail? macro-env))\\n        ;; (yin.k/outcome-of (f x)): the call's outcome as a value, not unwrapped\\n        (and (= operator 'yin.k/outcome-of) (outcomes? env))\\n        (compile-form (adapt-head env (first operands)) tail? env macro-env)\\n        ;; Native defn fallback: used only when no defmacro defn is in scope\\n        ;; and the form actually matches defn syntax.\\n                                          [index (conj acc c')]))\\n                                      [index []]\\n                                      (child-places row))]\\n                          (rebuild-row index row children')))]\\n                  (vswap! memo assoc a a')\\n                  [index a'])))]\\n      (go index root))))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Harvest and post-harvest (§3.2 steps 2, 3, 5; §3.5)\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(defn- harvest\\n  \\\"Initial harvest: iterate definitions in ordinal order; a declared one\\n   installs its lambda packet, a plain one removes the name. Last wins.\\n   A reserved name is never a definition key or a macro name (Rule R).\\\"\\n  [store index-of definitions]\\n  (reduce (fn [store {:keys [tree name value declared?]}]\\n            (when (vm/reserved-name? name)\\n              (vm/refuse-reserved! :definition-key name))\\n            (if declared?\\n              (assoc store name\\n                     (macro-entry (packet-of (index-of tree) value)\\n                                  vm/ast-contract))\\n              (dissoc store name)))\\n          store\\n          definitions))\\n\\nM\\tsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\\nM\\tsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md\\nM\\tsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\\nM\\tsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\\nM\\tsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc\\nA\\ttest/yin/vm/provenance_test.cljc\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_28\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The REPL probe confirms two authority leaks: raw single-form input can call the mint directly, and a macro can return the door for indirect application. The GC probes do isolate provenance-only reachability across all four lanes and demonstrate reclamation. I also confirmed that the mint accepts nil provenance, despite the consult’s non-nil requirement.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_29\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc | sed -n '50,60p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '3087,3093p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_29\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc | sed -n '50,60p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '3087,3093p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    50\\t  []\\n    51\\t  (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\\n    52\\t         :yang.frontend/revision \\\"c1-1\\\"\\n    53\\t         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\\n    54\\t\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t(defn- clojure-lower\\n    57\\t  [forms]\\n    58\\t  (if (= 1 (count forms))\\n    59\\t    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\\n    60\\t    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\\n  3087\\t               :operator {:type :variable, :name *}\\n  3088\\t               :operands [{:type :variable, :name x}\\n  3089\\t                          {:type :literal, :value 2}]}}\\\"\\n  3090\\t  [form]\\n  3091\\t  (compile-form form true {}))\\n  3092\\t\\n  3093\\t\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_30\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-11 17:02:53 GMT  \\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-12 00:02:53 +07 (+0700)\\n\\nReviewed `adb6af80..ff8b980a` against the complete consult. No files changed or suites run; verification used static inspection, cache-disabled lint, and targeted in-memory probes.\\n\\n**Findings**\\n\\n- **P1 — Single-form REPL input can invoke the privileged doors directly.** [module.cljc:438](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-vmprov/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:438) exposes the bindings, but the REPL’s [single-form lowering path](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-vmprov/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:58) calls `yang.clojure/compile`, bypassing `compile-program`’s reserved-prefix pre-pass. Reproduced `(cell/dsg__new-provenance 42 {:direct true})` returning a sealed cell through `repl/eval-input`, composed with the same Clojure binding as the standard catalog. Enforce source admission on this entry path while preserving trusted compiler construction.\\n\\n- **P1 — Constructor checks do not close macro-output admission.** [macro.cljc:964](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-vmprov/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:964) protects `yin/variable`, but [output admission:1467](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-vmprov/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1467) permits packets without construction provenance when they contain no applications. A guest macro returning a quoted, correctly addressed `:variable cell/dsg__new-provenance` packet passes expansion; `((leak) 42 {:forged true})` then mints authenticated provenance. Reproduced through both `expand-batch` plus evaluation and the REPL. Definition-target protection is also bypassable by assembling `yin/def` with `yin/application` instead of `yin/make-def`. Validate executable names at admission using trusted construction provenance, including references returned as values.\\n\\n- **P2 — The mint does not enforce non-nil provenance.** [module.cljc:419](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-vmprov/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:419) and [engine.cljc:2812](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-vmprov/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2812) accept nil and allocate `{:value 42, :seal …, :provenance nil}`. This violates the consult’s explicit precondition and makes the reader’s result indistinguishable from an unmarked cell. Reject nil before allocation and cover that refusal.\\n\\n**Verdicts against the numbered requirements**\\n\\n| Item | Verdict | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **1. Heap sibling/write preservation** | **PASS** | `heap-write` preserves sibling fields at engine:2450. `cell/get` exposes only value; `cell/set!` preserves provenance and seal without refusing marked cells. |\\n| **2. Doors and profiles** | **PARTIAL** | Atomic fresh allocation, authentication-before-read, nil for unauthenticated candidates, and profiles `[2]`/`[1]` are correct. Non-nil mint enforcement is missing. |\\n| **3. GC amendment** | **PASS** | Ordinary tracing at engine:2582, pinned tracing at :2628, and allocation roots at :2675/:2812 all include provenance as data. No automatic pinning or global rooting was added. |\\n| **4. Source/macro closure** | **FAIL** | Both authority bypasses above reproduce. |\\n| **5. Documentation** | **PASS** | `state.md:119` updates the entry shape; :123 explains optionality, privacy, preservation, and tracing. |\\n| **6. Test quality** | **PARTIAL** | Ordinary, pinned, allocation-triggered, and reclamation probes are substantive. Root-isolation probes confirmed payload retention depends on provenance across all four lanes. However, `provenance_test.cljc:275` calls only `m/invoke`, which returns **unvalidated** output; it never exercises expansion or indirect application and misses the demonstrated bypasses. |\\n\\n**Additional checks:** Exactly six files changed, one commit with parent `adb6af80`; the test filename is **`provenance_test.cljc`**, not the requested `.clj`. Kondo independently reports **0 errors, 1 warning**; the redundant `let` in `macro/construct` reproduces on the base at :768 and head at :780. Walker, semantic, de Bruijn stack, and register dispatch all preserve the engine-returned heap; no lane reconstructs individual entries.\\n\\n**REQUEST CHANGES**\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2495774,\"cached_input_tokens\":2387200,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":9578,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":1297}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
